This file lists the third-party software bundled into the built artifacts — the open
backend and frontend Docker images that make up the self-host Compose bundle — whose
license requires that an attribution or NOTICE be forwarded to recipients. Most MIT, BSD
and ISC dependencies are deliberately absent: absent an upstream NOTICE file of their
own they carry no Apache-2.0-style forwarding obligation, and enumerating every one of
them here would bury the entries that do carry one.
scripts/check-notice-coverage.sh is the standing check that this list still matches what
the images actually ship; its header documents what that does and does not prove.

FRONTEND FONTS AND ICONS
The frontend bundles the Geist, Geist Mono and Space Grotesk variable fonts
(@fontsource-variable/geist, @fontsource-variable/geist-mono,
@fontsource-variable/space-grotesk — all three the SIL Open Font License 1.1) and the
Lucide icon set (lucide-react — the ISC License). Neither license uses Apache-2.0's
NOTICE mechanism, so these are not attribution-forwarding entries in the sense the rest
of this file tracks. OFL 1.1 does require its own license text to travel with the font
files themselves, and Vite does not copy npm package license files into `dist` by
default, so the frontend build copies each package's own LICENSE into the served bundle
alongside the font binaries it ships. Deliberately no count is given here: the set grows
(Space Grotesk joined it when the wordmark's face moved off the Google Fonts
CDN to make the self-host egress claim true), and a number in this paragraph goes stale
without anything failing. scripts/check-notice-coverage.sh checks both halves against
the built frontend image — that this paragraph exists, and that license text travels
beside the fonts.

